From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:28:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Add the speakers

Link the AOP speaker back-end (DAI 3) to the six amps in a card of its
own, apple,j604-macaudio. The codecs are listed in the ADT provider
order, so each gets its native playback slot (LW1 0, RW1 1, LW2 2,
RW2 3, LT 4, RT 5); the idle masks are the ADT amp-tx-zd-config rows 0
and 1 (LW1 drives zeros into the right amps' sense slots, RW1 into the
left amps'), as on the J616s. The speaker-id straps are AP GPIO 4 and
13, with valid IDs 0 and 3 in the ADT.

The card id is AppleJ604, which the speaker protection profile and
the userspace audio configuration key on. The speaker volumes stay
locked (inaudible) until a protection daemon holds the lease and keeps
renewing it from the sense stream.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 38a7e6abaf..53ed27cb74 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -74,6 +74,44 @@
 		enable-active-high;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The speakers: the AOP firmware runs the stream (MCA cluster 0, one
+	 * serializer for all six amps, the J616s frame); macaudio links the AOP
+	 * audio component's speaker back-end (DAI 3) to the amps. The codecs
+	 * are listed in the ADT provider order, so each gets its native
+	 * playback slot (LW1 0, RW1 1, LW2 2, RW2 3, LT 4, RT 5). The idle masks
+	 * are the ADT amp-tx-zd-config rows 0 and 1 over the 24 sense byte
+	 * slots: LW1 drives zeros in the right amps' sense slots, RW1 in the
+	 * left amps'. The speaker-id straps are AP GPIO 4 and 13.
+	 */
+	sound: sound {
+		compatible = "apple,j604-macaudio", "apple,macaudio"; /* DTV-SPK-1 */
+		model = "MacBook Pro J604"; /* DTV-SPK-1b */
+		speaker-id-gpios = <&pinctrl_ap 4 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>,
+				   <&pinctrl_ap 13 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; /* DTV-SPK-4a, DTV-SPK-4b */
+		#address-cells = <1>;
+		#size-cells = <0>;
+
+		dai-link@0 {
+			reg = <0>;
+			link-name = "Speakers";
+			dai-tdm-idle-mode-0 = "zero";
+			dai-tdm-idle-mode-1 = "zero";
+			dai-tdm-slot-tx-idle-mask-0 = <0xf0f0f0>; /* DTV-SPK-6a */
+			dai-tdm-slot-tx-idle-mask-1 = <0x0f0f0f>; /* DTV-SPK-6b */
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&aop_audio 3>; /* DTV-SPK-7 */
+			};
+
+			codec {
+				sound-dai = <&speaker_left_woof1>, <&speaker_right_woof1>,
+					    <&speaker_left_woof2>, <&speaker_right_woof2>,
+					    <&speaker_left_tweet>, <&speaker_right_tweet>; /* DTV-SPK-8 */
+			};
+		};
+	};
+
 	/*
 	 * The headphone jack: the AOP audio component's jack back-end (DAI 4)
 	 * to the CS42L84, as a card of its own.
